// A fn-TYPE row is a GATE at the argument edge: a param typed
// `() -> Int with !WASI` meets each argument's row by SUBSUMPTION — the
// negation row judges, never binds — where the old equality-unify arm
// reported a false mismatch on EVERY closed-row argument (a Pure thunk
// "failed" the universe-minus row it plainly satisfies). The quiet thunk is
// admitted and the program runs, with ZERO mismatches.
//
// The noisy face — a printing thunk at the same edge — shared this file
// with the quiet one, and the program ran 42 beside the mismatch it
// reported. Arming E_EffectMismatch (2026-09-23) made that a refusal, so the
// noisy face is its own refusal fixture: mn-hof-row-gate-noisy.
// Expected: exit 42, no E_EffectMismatch.

fn quiet() = 42

fn accept_thunk(f: () -> Int with !WASI) -> Int with !WASI = f()

fn main() = accept_thunk(quiet)
